          "overview": "Session d02 spans five evidence-checking turns (d02-t2 to t6) on a single paper, 2004.00809 \"Mapping Languages and Demographics with Georeferenced Corpora\" — the only paper discussed, first and last. Recurring question: why does Twitter data better predict each country's language inventory? Evidence confirmed the abstract claim and supporting reasons (fewer missing languages, better North America/Oceania representation; r=0.60 vs r=0.49) plus candidate explanations (GDP-weighted wealthier population, urban-centered collection, commonness of English/Spanish), with no direct causal test. Unresolved references: no explicit hypothesis for the inventory advantage; open questions on false-positive sources (immigration, tourism, business; Russia case) and whether rural-centered collection yields the same bias.",
